  "question": "Can the case-scoped role rule be repaired to an importable standard, or must it be withdrawn?",
  "the_repair_attempted": "Widen the clause gate from 'more than one FINITE verb' to 'more than one verbal anchor of any kind, and no relative pronoun'. That is where the leakage analysis pointed: acl, xcomp, xcomp:result, advcl and nominal-internal nsubj are all clauses headed by something other than a finite verb, and a relative pronoun implies a clause whose own verb is often elided. Plus an agreement-based merge that collapses a modifier onto the argument it agrees with, to stop one argument being reported as two.",
